> Worldpay was owned by Royal Bank of Scotland. Bain Capital and Advent International bought a majority stake.
In late 2013 they took full ownership, valuing the company at over £2 billion.
This new ownership has lit a fire under the organisation who has now stepped up it’s operation, with a[ new] focus and a[ newly] energised management team.
Because Worldpay[ operate on such a] large scale it was important from the beginning to[ develop a core] idea which[ would] tell their whole story[ through their] branding. Yes they process transactions and provide payment solutions, but what[ they really] do is connect people.[ They] enable buyers and sellers to[ interact] with one another from anywhere in the world, seamlessly and with ease.
An exhaustive set[ of] iconography enables the brand to[ transcend] language[ across the 40+] countries[ they operate] in.
